<article class="env-lemma" id="05LE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05LE">Lemma <span data-tag="05LE">110.58.1</span>.</a> There exists a sheaf of abelian groups $G$ on $\mathit{Sch}_{\acute{e}tale}$ with the following properties </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$G(X) = 0$ whenever $\dim (X) < n$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$G(X)$ is not zero if $\dim (X) \geq n$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
if $X \subset X'$ is a thickening, then $G(X) = G(X')$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
